{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Face to face.</b> I do not know whether the Exalted One humbled Himself or the lowly one exalted himself. Rabbi Yehoshua said: as it were, the Exalted One bent Himself down, as it is written 'and YHWH descended in the cloud,' and this was from the third set of forty days onward." "<b>And he returned to the camp.</b> Here Rashi explained: on the 17th of Tammuz the tablets were broken, and on the 18th he burned the calf and judged the sinners, and on the 19th he went up, etc. This is difficult, for in the portion of Yitro and in the portion of Eikev he himself explained that on the 18th he went up. He did not move from inside the tent to come to the camp."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:39.492337196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}